  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the pathogenesis of SNU-387 through a series of mechanistic links that converge on the P2X purinoceptor family. The drug is directly targeted by LOUCY, a compound that acts as a target of multiple P2X purinoceptors, including P2X1 and P2X7. These receptors are known to mediate cellular signaling through adenosine triphosphate (ATP) binding, which can lead to various cellular responses, including inflammation and cell death. The presence of LOUCY as a common target of multiple P2X receptors suggests a potential role in modulating cellular activity in SNU-387, a cell line that may be sensitive to these signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which palmarumycin CP18 influences SNU-387, potentially through the modulation of P2X receptor activity. The evidence supports a direct relationship between palmarumycin CP18 and SNU-387, mediated through the P2X receptor family, with LOUCY serving as a critical bridge in this interaction.",
